# Local runtime state written next to the project. Never a source file, never
# commit it.
# Scoped to the repo root only — an unscoped "data/" also matched src/data/**,
# silently dropping the Instagram source of truth (types.ts, instagram-posts.json)
# at commit time. Confirmed via `git check-ignore -v`.
/data/

# Local design-tooling state. Kept out of the repository on purpose: this is a
# public site, and its contents are an AI coding assistant's working files, not
# part of the product. Everything here is re-installable from
# Carebridge-internal/docs/team/ROUND3-PLAN.md, "Installing Impeccable".
.claude/
.impeccable/

# Impeccable's product/design working files (root only) -- same reasoning as
# above: AI working files, not product source, never committed to this
# public repo.
/PRODUCT.md
/DESIGN.md

# Team working papers -- internal process reports, screenshots and evidence.
# Removed from the public repo once already (cb987f6); ignored here so that
# doesn't have to happen again every round.
/reports/

# The team's working documents: the kit (briefs, plans, rules), the verification
# evidence and harness, the diagrams. The MASTER copy lives outside this
# repository, in D:\桌面\Carebridge-internal -- nothing here belongs in a public
# repo. It is mirrored into this tree anyway, because the team runs with its
# working directory here and every brief, rule and kickoff addresses these files
# relative to that directory ("docs/team/prompts/...", "docs/TEAM-RULES.md",
# "STATUS.md"). Without the mirror those paths do not exist and a member stalls --
# or improvises from a brief that arrived truncated, which is what happened in
# Round 3 (reports/fixer-T15-T16.md, line 22).
#
#   keep in sync with : node docs/team/sync-kit.mjs          (master -> here)
#   take the team's work back : node docs/team/sync-kit.mjs --pull
#   verify : node docs/team/sync-kit.mjs --check   (also run by check-kit.mjs)
#
# Scoped to the repo root on purpose: an unscoped "team/" would also hide any
# src/**/team/** that ever appears. The two real docs in docs/ -- DEPLOYMENT.md
# and INSTAGRAM.md -- are tracked product documentation and stay tracked.
/docs/team/
/docs/verify/
/docs/diagrams/
/docs/plans/
/docs/TEAM-RULES.md
/docs/PLACEHOLDERS.md
/STATUS.md
